/*******************************************************************************
* Instrument: SOLEIL_PX1
*
* %Identification
* Written by: E. Farhi
* Date: 2026-10-03
* Origin: Synchrotron SOLEIL
* %INSTRUMENT_SITE: SOLEIL
*
* The PROXIMA-1 (PX1) MX beam-line at Synchrotron SOLEIL.
*
* %Description
* PROXIMA-1 (PX1) is one of the two macromolecular crystallography (MX)
* beam-lines at Synchrotron SOLEIL, operational since March 2008. The
* end-station is dedicated to bio-molecular crystallography, with a layout
* designed to favour anomalous diffraction data recording and studies of
* crystals with large unit cell dimensions (thanks to the low horizontal
* divergence of the beam at the sample). The X-ray photons originate from an
* in-vacuum U20 undulator, and are modulated through a liquid-nitrogen-cooled
* Si(111) channel-cut monochromator and a pair of Kirkpatrick-Baez (KB)
* focusing mirrors. The standard energy range is 6.5-15 keV, with 12.67 keV
* set as the reference energy. The beam size at the sample is 120 (H) x 20 (V)
* um FWHM uncollimated (40 x 20 um when collimated), with a flux of
* 3.8e11 photons/s at 12.67 keV for a 500 mA ring current (2.1e11 when
* collimated). The end-station hosts a chi-geometry three-axis goniometer
* (SmarGon), a KETEK silicon drift detector for X-ray spectroscopy, an Oxford
* Cryosystems 700-series cryo-stream, a CATS sample exchange robot (48 samples),
* and the fast single-photon-counting pixel-array detector EigerX-16M,
* routinely used at 100 Hz.
*
* This is a simplified model with an undulator, a Si(111) channel-cut
* monochromator, a KB mirror pair, a sample stage and a detector. It is
* adapted from the SOLEIL_PX2a.instr model (M. Savko, E. Farhi), using:
*  - L.M.G. Chavas et al., "PROXIMA-1 beamline for macromolecular
*    crystallography measurements at Synchrotron SOLEIL",
*    J. Synchrotron Rad. (2021). 28, 970-976 (layout, Table 1, Fig. 1
*    element distances);
*  - the publication supporting information (measured U20 harmonics at the
*    5.5 mm minimum gap);
*  - the SOLEIL PROXIMA-1 web page (U20 with 100 periods of 20 mm);
*  - the SOLEIL PX1 synoptique drawings (TEC-CI-PL-0356 and PX1_SYNOPTIQUE).
*
* List of important beamline elements. Distances are given from the center of
* the undulator (from Chavas et al. 2021, Fig. 1; hutch boundary C04/CX1 is
* approximate).
*
* Element            | Distance (m) | Description | Hutch
* -------------------|--------------|-------------|--------------------
* U20 undulator      | 0.0          | In-vacuum undulator, 100 periods x 20 mm (magnetic length 2 m), minimum gap 5.5 mm, K_max=1.66. Odd harmonics give access to 5-20 keV. Undulator is tapered (30 um) in operation. | Source/Front-end
* MBS, WBS           | ~10-16       | Main beam shutter, white-beam slits, beam-defining mask 0.27 (H) x 0.47 (V) mrad. Not modeled. | Front-end
* CCM                | 16.397       | Liquid-nitrogen-cooled Si(111) single-crystal channel-cut monochromator with piezo pitch fine tuning. First optical element seen by the beam. Channel gap 6 mm (assumed, as PX2a). | OH
* SeS                | 18.5         | Secondary slits; define the footprint on the KB mirrors. | OH
* DSS                | ~19          | Downstream safety shutter. Not modeled. | OH
* KB (V)             | 21.45        | Vertical-focusing KB mirror, first-generation Rh-coated glass, grazing angle 4.1 mrad. | OH
* KB (H)             | 21.9         | Horizontal-focusing KB mirror, same coating/angle. Beam at sample: 120 (H) x 20 (V) um FWHM uncollimated, 40 x 20 um collimated; divergence 0.26 (H) x 0.48 (V) mrad. Mirror separation 0.45 m assumed. | OH
* DT                 | ~22          | Diagnostic tools, diamond CVD X-ray beam positioning monitor. Not modeled. | OH/EH
* ES                 | ~23          | Experimental slits. Not modeled. | EH
* SaS                | ~23.7        | Sample slits; collimation of the beam down to 40 x 20 um. Not modeled. | EH
* FS                 | ~23.8        | Fast shutter. Not modeled. | EH
* SG (sample)        | 23.846       | Sample position: SmarGon chi-geometry 3-axis goniometer, Oxford Cryosystems 700 series, KETEK SDD, CATS sample changer (3 Unipucks, 48 samples). | EH
* PAD (detector)     | 23.846+det_dist | EigerX-16M single-photon-counting pixel-array detector, 311 x 328 mm2, 75 um pixels, routinely used at 100 Hz. Sample-to-detector distance 0.096-1.55 m. | EH
*
* Notes:
* - Undulator harmonics: at the fixed minimum gap of 5.5 mm (K=1.66), the
*   measured spectrum shows harmonics 4 to 10 at 6.006, 7.558, 9.026, 10.558,
*   12.058, 13.622 and 15.084 keV, i.e. a fundamental at E1=1.507 keV. At the
*   default E0=12.67 keV the undulator is tuned onto the 7th harmonic, which
*   requires K=1.4028 (gap slightly opened). The K parameter is exposed; when
*   changing E0, adjust K to stay on a harmonic: with lu=20 mm and Ee=2.75 GeV
*   the fundamental is E1 = 3.591/(1+K*K/2) keV, i.e. K = sqrt(2*(3.591/E1 - 1))
*   with E1=E0/harmonic. Available odd harmonics (3,5,7,...) cover 5-20 keV.
* - KB focusing: the default radii focus the source (undulator) onto the
*   sample, using the cylindrical mirror formula R = 2*p*q/((p+q)*sin(grazing angle)):
*   vfm_radius = 2*21.45*2.396/((21.45+2.396)*4.1e-3)      = 1051 m
*   hfm_radius = 2*21.90*1.946/((21.90+1.946)*4.1e-3)      =  872 m
*   In reality the KB pair focuses slightly downstream of the sample, onto
*   the detector surface when placed at the most common distance (about
*   0.46 m past the sample for a 2 A outer-shell resolution); use
*   vfm_radius=1230 and hfm_radius=1058 to model this configuration.
*   The real beam size is dominated by the mirror figure errors (first
*   generation KB), not by the source demagnification, so the simulated
*   focus is sharper than the measured 120 (H) x 20 (V) um.
* - The front-end mask, shutters, slits, attenuators, Be/Kapton windows,
*   beam positioning monitors, the fast shutter and the undulator taper mode
*   are not modeled. The transfocator listed in some PX1 synoptiques has no
*   published parameters and is not modeled either.
* - Electron beam sizes are nominal SOLEIL short straight section values
*   (beta_x=2.19 m, beta_y=1.09 m, emittance 3.74 nm rad, 1% coupling).
*
* %Example: E0=12.67 K=1.4028 sample="adrenaline.lau" SPLITs=1500 Detector: psd4pi_I=1.75e+12
* %Example: E0=12.67 sample="adrenaline.lau" SPLITs=4200 Detector: EigerX16M_I=3.8e+15
*
* %Parameters
* E0:    [keV] Energy selected at the Undulator (reference energy 12.67 keV, standard range 6.5-15 keV).
* K:     [1] Undulator deflection parameter (K=1.4028: 7th harmonic at 12.67 keV; K_max=1.66 at 5.5 mm gap).
* vfm_radius: [m] vertically focusing mirror radius (tangential).
* hfm_radius: [m] horizontally focusing mirror radius (tangential).
* mirror_grazing_angle: [rad] Tilt angle of the KB mirrors (4.1 mrad).
* det_dist: [m] Sample-to-detector distance (0.096-1.55 m).
* sample: [str] Sample structure file, LAU/CIF format.
* rotX:  [deg] Sample rotation around X
* rotY:  [deg] Sample rotation around Y
* rotZ:  [deg] Sample rotation around Z
* SPLITs:[1]   Ray splitting factor at the sample.
*
* %Link
* https://www.synchrotron-soleil.fr/en/beamlines/proxima-1
*
* %End
*******************************************************************************/

DEFINE INSTRUMENT SOLEIL_PX1(
  E0=12.67, K=1.4028, vfm_radius=1051, hfm_radius=872,
  mirror_grazing_angle=4.1e-3, det_dist=0.2,
  string sample="adrenaline.lau",
  rotX=0, rotY=0, rotZ=0, SPLITs=10)
DEPENDENCY " -DMCSX_REFL_SLIST_SIZE=1024 "
DECLARE
%{
    double calculated_angle;
%}

USERVARS %{
    int    flag_hfm;
    int    flag_vfm;
%}

INITIALIZE
%{
  /* Si(111) Bragg angle for the channel-cut monochromator */
  double arg=  12398.42*sqrt(3)/(2*5.4309*E0*1e3);
  if (fabs(arg) > 1)
    exit(fprintf(stderr, "ERROR: Monochromator can not reach this energy (arg=%g > 1)\n",
      arg));
  calculated_angle = RAD2DEG*asin(arg);
  /* Ensure that we are running with at least 1e7 neutrons/core if not 'displaying' */
  #ifndef USE_MPI
  #define mpi_node_count 1
  #endif
  if (!mcdotrace) {
    if (mcget_ncount()<=1e7) {
      MPI_MASTER(printf("This instrument needs higher statistics to converge. Increasing your ncount=%llu to ",mcget_ncount()));
      mcset_ncount(mpi_node_count*1e7);
      MPI_MASTER(printf("%llu\n",mcget_ncount()));
    }
  }
%}

TRACE

REMOVABLE COMPONENT Origin = Progress_bar()
AT (0,0,0) ABSOLUTE

// Undulator U20 (in vacuum): 100 periods of 20 mm, minimum gap 5.5 mm.
// K=1.4028 puts the 7th harmonic at the reference energy E0=12.67 keV
// (fundamental E1=1.81 keV). At the minimum gap of 5.5 mm, K_max=1.66
// (fundamental 1.507 keV, harmonics up to 15 keV). E1st is computed from
// K and lu. dist is the distance to the first optical element (the CCM).
COMPONENT undulator = Undulator(
    E0=E0,
    dE=.1,
    Ee=2.75,
    dEe=0.001,
    Ie=0.5,
    K=K,
    Nper=100,
    lu=2.0e-2,
    sigey=6.4e-6,
    sigex=90.5e-6,
    sigepx=41.3e-6,
    sigepy=5.9e-6,
    dist=16.397)
AT (0, 0, 0) RELATIVE PREVIOUS

// Channel_cut Si(111) monochromator (CCM) at 16.397 m -------------------------
// LN2-cooled, first optical element. Channel gap 6 mm.
COMPONENT bragg_crystal_location = Arm()
AT (0,0,16.397) RELATIVE PREVIOUS

COMPONENT bragg_crystal = Bragg_crystal(
    crystal_type=2)
AT (0, 0, 0) RELATIVE PREVIOUS
ROTATED (-calculated_angle, 0, 0) RELATIVE PREVIOUS

COMPONENT arm = Arm()
AT (0, 0, 0) RELATIVE PREVIOUS
ROTATED (-calculated_angle, 0, 0) RELATIVE PREVIOUS

COMPONENT bragg_crystal_two = Bragg_crystal(
    crystal_type=2)
AT (0, 0.006, calculated_angle ? 0.006/tan(calculated_angle*DEG2RAD) : 0) RELATIVE bragg_crystal
ROTATED (calculated_angle, 0, 0) RELATIVE PREVIOUS

COMPONENT arm_two = Arm()
AT (0, 0, 0) RELATIVE bragg_crystal_two
ROTATED (calculated_angle, 0, 0) RELATIVE bragg_crystal_two

COMPONENT bragg_crystal_out = E_monitor(Emin=E0-.1, Emax=E0+.1, nE=512,
  xwidth=0.1, yheight=0.1)
AT(0,0,0.2) RELATIVE PREVIOUS

// Secondary slits (SeS) at 18.5 m --------------------------------------------
COMPONENT secondary_slits = Slit(xwidth=1e-3, yheight=1e-3)
AT (0, 0, 18.5-16.397) RELATIVE arm_two

// KB pair ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// Vertically focusing mirror at 21.45 m, horizontally focusing at 21.9 m.
// Rh-coated glass, grazing angle 4.1 mrad. Radii: see header notes.
// could use Mirror_elliptic

// KB 1st mirror: vertical focusing, at 2.4 m from the sample
COMPONENT vfm_location = Monitor_nD(xwidth=0.01, yheight=0.01, options="x y", bins=100)
AT (0,0,21.45-18.5) RELATIVE secondary_slits

COMPONENT vfm_in_xz_plane = Arm()
AT (0,0,0) RELATIVE vfm_location
ROTATED (0,0,-90) RELATIVE vfm_location // YZ -> XZ

COMPONENT vfm = Mirror_curved(
  coating="Rh.txt",
  length=450e-3,
  width=0.1,
  radius=vfm_radius)
AT (0,0,0) RELATIVE vfm_location
ROTATED (0,-mirror_grazing_angle,0) RELATIVE vfm_in_xz_plane
EXTEND %{
  flag_vfm=SCATTERED;
%}

COMPONENT vfm_takeoff = COPY(vfm_location)
AT (0,0,0) RELATIVE vfm_in_xz_plane
ROTATED (-2*mirror_grazing_angle, 0, 0) RELATIVE vfm_location

// KB 2nd mirror: horizontal focusing, at 1.95 m from the sample
COMPONENT hfm_location = COPY(vfm_location)
AT (0,0,21.9-21.45) RELATIVE vfm_takeoff

COMPONENT hfm = Mirror_curved(
  coating="Rh.txt",
  length=450e-3,
  width=0.1,
  radius=hfm_radius)
AT (0,0,0) RELATIVE hfm_location
ROTATED (0,-mirror_grazing_angle,0) RELATIVE hfm_location
EXTEND %{
  flag_hfm=SCATTERED;
%}

COMPONENT hfm_takeoff = COPY(vfm_location)
AT (0,0,0) RELATIVE hfm_location
ROTATED (0,-2*mirror_grazing_angle,0) RELATIVE hfm_location

// Sample ----------------------------------------------------------------------
// We centre the beam after the KB. Sample position (SG) at 23.846 m.
COMPONENT sample_stage = Arm()
AT (0,0,23.846-21.9) RELATIVE hfm_takeoff
EXTEND %{
  if (!flag_hfm || !flag_vfm) ABSORB;
%}

COMPONENT sample_monitor = Monitor_nD(
  xwidth = 0.01, yheight = 0.01,
  options = "x y", bins=100)
AT (0, 0, 0) RELATIVE sample_stage

SPLIT SPLITs COMPONENT sample = Single_crystal(reflections=sample, material_datafile="NULL",
  radius = .5e-4, yheight = 5e-3, p_transmit = 0, mosaic=0.1, order=1)
  AT (0, 0, 0) RELATIVE sample_stage
  ROTATED (rotX,rotY,rotZ) RELATIVE sample_stage
EXTEND %{
  if (!SCATTERED) ABSORB;
%}

COMPONENT psd4pi = PSD_monitor_4PI(
    nx = 180, ny = 180, filename = "psd4pi", radius = 0.1, restore_xray = 1)
AT (0, 0, 0) RELATIVE sample

// Detector: EigerX-16M pixel-array detector, 311 x 328 mm2, 75 um pixels
COMPONENT EigerX16M = PSD_monitor(
  nx=4150, ny=4371,
  xwidth = 311.2e-3,
  yheight= 327.8e-3,
  filename="EigerX16M.dat"
)
AT (0,0,det_dist) RELATIVE sample_stage

END
